  "verbalization": "Vinblastine is linked to TE-11 through a series of molecular interactions involving a common target molecule, 3-[2-[4-[5-[2-(2,3-Dihydroxyphenyl)ethyl]-2-hydroxyphenoxy]phenyl]ethyl]benzene-1,2-diol. This molecule is identified as the target of vinblastine, MKN-7, and G-401, all of which are implicated in the targeting of TE-11. The evidence suggests that vinblastine exerts its biological effects by first binding to and modulating the activity of this shared target, which in turn influences the function of TE-11. The consistent presence of this target molecule across multiple pathways supports a mechanism where vinblastine acts through a common molecular interface to affect TE-11. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of this compound as a critical mediator in the interaction between vinblastine and TE-11, emphasizing the importance of this shared target in the drug's mechanism of action.",
